  "rai:dataCollection": "Annotations were created from publicly available YouTube MovieCLIPS source videos. The release contains source URLs and annotation metadata only; it does not redistribute video files.",
  "rai:dataUseCases": "Research evaluation of multimodal video understanding, speech grounding, speaker-face grounding, and cinematic reasoning.",
  "rai:dataLimitations": "The source videos are movie clips and may overrepresent Western/Hollywood cinematic style. Availability of source URLs can change over time. Users must retrieve videos under applicable platform terms and copyright constraints. Two grounding intervals use estimated durations, eight revised MCQ distractor sets have not been rechecked against the videos, and two duplicate-question pairs are retained; see datasets/README.md.",
  "rai:personalSensitiveInformation": "The annotations include normalized face boxes for visible actors in public movie clips. No biometric identity templates are released.",
  "rai:annotationProtocol": "Annotations were generated through automatic speech/face preprocessing, model-assisted proposal generation, adversarial distractor refinement, and human verification.",
  "rai:maintenancePlan": "Dataset versions and evaluation code are maintained in this repository. Annotation and evaluation issues can be reported through the repository issue tracker.",
  "rai:dataBiases": "CineMME is built from publicly available movie clips, so it may reflect selection biases in Hollywood and mainstream film production, including genre, language, geography, demographic representation, and cinematic conventions.",
  "rai:dataSocialImpact": "The dataset supports reproducible evaluation of multimodal systems, but misuse could include overclaiming real-world social understanding from movie scenes or using face-box annotations outside benchmark evaluation. The release limits data to annotations and source URLs and does not provide biometric templates or video copies.",
  "rai:hasSyntheticData": true,
  "prov:wasDerivedFrom": [
    {
      "@type": "sc:CreativeWork",
      "name": "YouTube MovieCLIPS source videos",
      "url": "https://www.youtube.com/@MOVIECLIPS"
